{title: I Was Blind, and Now I See}
{subtitle: John 9:1–41}
{key: Ab}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] |
| [Ab] | ×8

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Born in the dark, I [Db]sat by the road
[Ab]Begging for coins with a [Eb]heavy load
[Fm]He spat on the ground and [Db]he made some clay
He put [Ab]it on my eyes and he said, go [Eb]wash it a[Ab]way
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I went to the pool and I [Db]washed my face
[Ab]And light came pouring [Eb]into that place
The [Fm]neighbors asked, isn't this the [Db]beggar man
The leaders [Ab]asked me who and how, they did [Eb]not under[Ab]stand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Whether he is a [Db]sinner I do not [Ab]know
One [Eb]thing I do know
[Ab]I was [Db]blind, and now I see
[Ab]I was [Eb]blind, and now I [Ab]see
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
They questioned my mother, they [Db]questioned me twice
[Ab]They wanted an answer to fit [Eb]their device
[Fm]But all I can tell you [Db]is what he has done
He [Ab]opened my eyes and I'm [Eb]seeing the sun
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Ab]Whether he is a [Db]sinner I do not [Ab]know
One [Eb]thing I do know
[Ab]I was [Db]blind, and now I see
[Ab]I was [Eb]blind, and now I [Ab]see
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
I am the light of the world
I was blind, and now I see
{end_of_verse}
